  "printed": "Rom. v. 20",
  "page": 110,
  "line": 9,
  "situation": "The plate cites `Rom. v. 2`, and the verse is Rom. v. 20. *Superabundavit gratia* is the Vulgate of Romans v. 20 word for word; v. 2 is *access by faith into this grace*, a different sentence. And the volume proves it against itself: printed 103 cites `Rom. v. 20` correctly. A dropped nought, kept as printed — the fifth place in this edition where one page corrects another.",
